Z||000000||DaveL||07-12-2000||02:36 PM||||What would happen if on or both of the gears in the auto transaxle were stripped or borderline? On the THM 125, what does it control? Anything besides the speedometer?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||07-12-2000||04:41 PM||||The governer is part of shift timing. The top of it's shaft drives the VSS. A dead or inaccurate VSS will majorly screw up performance. It's used by the ECM as well as the speedo.||||reg||1
